# Use-Case Catalog

This catalog provides an overview of AI use cases relevant to the automotive industry.  
Each use case is evaluated based on feasibility, data availability, expected business value, and integration complexity.

---

## 1. Predictive Maintenance
**Goal:** Reduce downtime and maintenance costs by predicting component failures.  
**Data Required:** Sensor logs, error codes, maintenance history.  
**Value:** High  
**Feasibility:** Medium  
**Notes:** Strong candidate for GPU acceleration.

---

## 2. Quality Inspection (Computer Vision)
**Goal:** Detect defects in production using image or video analysis.  
**Data Required:** High-resolution images, defect labels.  
**Value:** Very High  
**Feasibility:** Medium  
**Notes:** Ideal for NVIDIA Omniverse + CV pipelines.

---

## 3. Logistics Optimization
**Goal:** Optimize material flow, routing, and warehouse operations.  
**Data Required:** ERP data, transport logs, inventory levels.  
**Value:** High  
**Feasibility:** High  
**Notes:** Strong ROI, often underestimated.

---

## 4. E/E Architecture Analysis
**Goal:** Identify inconsistencies, redundancies, and risks in electrical/electronic architectures.  
**Data Required:** Architecture models, component metadata, dependencies.  
**Value:** Medium  
**Feasibility:** Medium  
**Notes:** Your domain expertise makes this a unique differentiator.

---

## 5. Document AI (Automated Processing)
**Goal:** Extract structured information from technical documents, PDFs, and specifications.  
**Data Required:** PDFs, text corpora, templates.  
**Value:** Medium  
**Feasibility:** High  
**Notes:** Quick wins possible with LLM-based pipelines.

---

## 6. Use-Case Scoring Engine
**Goal:** Systematically evaluate AI use cases based on value, feasibility, and data readiness.  
**Data Required:** Metadata about processes, data availability, business KPIs.  
**Value:** Very High  
**Feasibility:** High  
**Notes:** Core component of the AI Enablement Layer.
